    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d704">

                <pb facs="0624" n="548" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg548"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/18171</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Bowman to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Frontera</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 16, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Mayor of Frontera has received instructions from Governor to organize the
                    citizens for defense, treating the question of a war as a certainty but not yet
                    declared. Americans have not been ill-treated though usual threats from
                    irresponsible people have been made.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
